1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,364
Neurosurgeon Bench.

2
00:00:01,364 --> 00:00:06,135
Can a language model write, or surgically edit, the weights of a neural network directly, with

3
00:00:06,135 --> 00:00:07,606
no gradients and no training?

4
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:10,803
This is a short tour of the benchmark and what it shows so far.

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,713
Models are good at writing code.

6
00:00:13,713 --> 00:00:15,088
Can they write weights?

7
00:00:15,088 --> 00:00:19,034
Track W asks a model to hand write every weight of a tiny network.

8
00:00:19,034 --> 00:00:23,278
Track E gives it a corrupted policy and lets it make at most ten edits.

9
00:00:23,278 --> 00:00:27,821
Track S asks it to steer an open weight model by editing individual neurons.

10
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,153
The model sees a task description and replies with numbers.

11
00:00:32,153 --> 00:00:37,406
The harness loads them into a small MLP, runs the game with no further learning, and compares

12
00:00:37,406 --> 00:00:40,230
the score to a random floor and a C E M reference.

13
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:43,393
Matching the reference scores fifty, random scores zero.

14
00:00:44,390 --> 00:00:49,596
Track W, round one, scored 71 models on three games: cart pole, mountain car and catch.

15
00:00:49,596 --> 00:00:51,092
The median index is 47.3.

16
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:56,059
28 models reach fifty or more, meaning they match the reference, and 18 score zero.

17
00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:00,509
The best models cluster just above fifty.

18
00:01:00,509 --> 00:01:02,360
The top index is 52.2.

19
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:07,492
On the three easy games, the ceiling is simply the reference.

20
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:14,802
Per game, 45 models reach forty or more on cart pole, 42 on mountain car, and 46 on catch.

21
00:01:14,802 --> 00:01:20,133
Hand written weights are within reach for many models on easy control tasks.

22
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:23,821
The harder v2 tasks separate models.

23
00:01:23,821 --> 00:01:30,846
In a pilot of 6 models over 8 tasks, only two models score well on pong, pendulum and an eight

24
00:01:30,846 --> 00:01:34,658
bit parity circuit; the best overall index is 54.4.

25
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:41,772
Track E, sparse weight editing: six weights of a trained policy are corrupted and the model may

26
00:01:41,772 --> 00:01:42,737
make ten edits.

27
00:01:42,737 --> 00:01:48,077
Of the pilot models, two achieve full recovery on cart pole, and one also on catch.

28
00:01:48,077 --> 00:01:50,393
Pong and pendulum are not recovered.

29
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:51,872
Caveats.

30
00:01:51,872 --> 00:01:55,846
The v2 and edit results are pilots of six models, one sample each.

31
00:01:55,846 --> 00:02:01,086
The reference is C E M, so the index is not comparable to the original P P O based one.

32
00:02:01,086 --> 00:02:03,253
Track S has code but no results yet.

33
00:02:03,253 --> 00:02:07,409
And an index of zero means no better than random weights were scored.

34
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:12,171
Code, configs and results are in the repo.

